    {
      "id": "e27616cbe5b9e9a0fd6edf87d6e2a596baaffcf8",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1516671260,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Behavior after this change:\n\n- **Clear display filter** button works fine\n- **Apply display filter** button still has the text mouse cursor when the button is not available (= when there is nothing to apply)\n    - except that it is clickable when Wireshark is first started (goes to \"unavailable\" mode when clicking with no display filter)",
          "author": {
            "id": 7558431,
            "username": "markkuleinio",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Markku Leiniö",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/7558431/avatar.png?v=1789663372",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/markkuleinio"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-08-17T08:54:11.192Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-08-17T12:22:12.372Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 243670617,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2023-08-17T12:22:12.372Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 11724,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 1516869662,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The Apply display filter button has always been clickable when Wireshark is first started, because an empty display filter is a legal filter - when you click it, it applies the empty display filter, and then goes to unavailable mode because it has just applied the filter in the edit. Similarly, if you change what is in the edit and restore it to the currently set filter - whether empty or a set filter like \"ip\", the button will become clickable, even if the filter in the edit is the current filter.\n\nThere might be some way to change it.\n\nThe text cursor not changing when the button is disabled is by design in Qt - https://bugreports.qt.io/browse/QTBUG-38077\n\nIt's possible to do a complicated workaround to not really disable a widget but make it seem disabled (changing the icon mode, rejecting events, etc.), see https://stackoverflow.com/questions/76012772/setcursorqcursorqt-forbiddencursor-does-not-work-on-disabled-qlineedit for an example in PyQt. I personally don't think it's worth it.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-08-17T10:51:49.349Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-08-17T12:22:12.372Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 243670617,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
